        "seo_questions": {
          "bn": "",
          "de": "",
          "en": "What are the two types of believers (Mumineen) according to Imam al-Sadiq (عليه السلام) in al-Kafi, and how do they differ in intercession on the Day of Judgment?",
          "es": "",
          "fa": "",
          "fr": "",
          "id": "",
          "ru": "",
          "tr": "",
          "ur": "",
          "zh": ""
        },
        "summaries": {
          "bn": "",
          "de": "",
          "en": "Imam Abu 'Abdillah (عليه السلام) divides believers into two ranks: the steadfast believer who fulfills the Divine Covenant — as referenced in Quran 33:23 — and who is thereby shielded from the terrors of both this world and the Hereafter, possessing the rank to intercede for others without requiring intercession. The second is the wavering believer, likened to a plant stalk that bends and then straightens, who remains susceptible to worldly and eschatological tribulations and depends upon the intercession of others for salvation.",
          "es": "",
          "fa": "",
          "fr": "",
          "id": "",
          "ru": "",
          "tr": "",
          "ur": "",
          "zh": ""
        },
